{
  "name": "Momentum Confluence \u2014 Low Realized-Vol Regime Gate",
  "rationale": "Thesis: short (6d) + medium (16d) momentum agreement is more reliable when realized volatility is low \u2014 high vol drowns trend in noise and inflates whipsaw cost at 10bps taker. Disconfirmer: the vol_realized ceiling must add value over unconditional confluence; if high-vol entries earn the same net of fees, the vol regime gate is decorative and this is plain momentum.",
  "catalyst": "Dual-horizon momentum aligns while realized vol is below a fitted ceiling.",
